{"theme_date" : "2026-10-08", "rows" : [{"name" : "CAD/PLM & 3D Design Engineering Software", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["ADSK","PTC"], "score" : 74.2, "description" : "PTC is surging on Schneider Electric’s agreed $22.6 billion all-cash takeover at $205 per share, a 42.3% premium to its prior close. Autodesk is rising in sympathy as investors treat the deal’s premium as a higher valuation benchmark for engineering and industrial software peers.", "rs_avg" : 88.3}, {"name" : "Liquid Biopsy & Molecular Cancer Diagnostics Testing", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : "Genomics & DNA Sequencing Tools", "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["NTRA","CDNA","GRAL","CSTL"], "score" : 79.6, "description" : "GRAL is benefiting from the FDA advisory panel’s favorable vote on its Galleri cancer-screening test; NTRA from positive Signatera data presented at ASTRO and a raised Citi price target. CDNA’s rally reflects strong quarterly growth, raised guidance and finalized Medicare coverage, while CSTL is getting a lift from new DecisionDx-Melanoma study data.", "rs_avg" : 99.1}, {"name" : "U.S. Oil Refiners & Refining Margin Expansion", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["PBF","CVI","MPC","VLO","DINO","PSX"], "score" : 79.5, "description" : "The rally is being driven by exceptionally strong refining margins, especially diesel cracks, as Middle East/Russia-related disruptions and low product inventories keep fuel supplies tight. Investors are repricing refiners for higher profits; there doesn’t appear to be one company-specific headline driving the group.", "rs_avg" : 99}, {"name" : "International Telecom & Cross-Border Communications Services", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["IDT","VEON"], "score" : 79.3, "description" : "VEON’s move is being driven mainly by its 10-year Amdocs deal to modernize and manage its Eurasian technology operations, with AI and cost-predictability benefits. A reported increase in its planned Pakistan investment to $1.5 billion may also be adding optimism.", "rs_avg" : 98.6}, {"name" : "Specialty Biopharma Clinical & Commercial Breakouts (Retinal, Pulmonary, Dermatology)", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["UTHR","MANE","KOD"], "score" : 79.3, "description" : "KOD is rising on its positive Phase 3 DAYBREAK results in wet AMD and this week’s announcement that the data will be presented at the AAO meeting. UTHR gained after a court ruled Liquidia’s Yutrepia infringed UTHR’s patent, potentially limiting competition. MANE’s move appears to be trading-driven; no clear company-specific catalyst surfaced.", "rs_avg" : 98.5}, {"name" : "Crude & Product Tanker Shipping", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["INSW","DHT","NAT","TEN","FRO","ECO"], "score" : 79, "description" : "The rally is being driven by a sharp spike in tanker freight rates as attacks and disruption around the Strait of Hormuz and Bab el-Mandeb tighten vessel availability and raise security premiums. VLCC rates have surged above $1 million a day, boosting expected earnings across these tanker operators.", "rs_avg" : 98.1}, {"name" : "Life Sciences & Healthcare Data/CRM Platforms", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["VEEV","TEM","DOCS"], "score" : 79, "description" : "TEM has the clearest catalyst: FDA 510(k) clearance for its ECG-MR heart-valve detection AI, amplified by a Guggenheim price-target hike. VEEV is riding AI/data momentum, including Servier’s global OpenData rollout and news that its DQS has processed data for over 1 million trial subjects. DOCS has no clear fresh positive catalyst in the available news; a recent analyst Buy reaffirmation may be helping, but the evidence is weaker.", "rs_avg" : 98}, {"name" : "Software Development & DevOps Collaboration Platforms", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["GTLB","FROG","TEAM"], "score" : 79, "description" : "The main catalyst is a broad rebound in software stocks as investors grow less worried that AI will disrupt the sector and earnings expectations improve. There’s no clear single company-specific headline linking TEAM, GTLB, and FROG; AI product momentum and recent execution are supportive background factors.", "rs_avg" : 98}, {"name" : "Oilfield Services & Offshore Energy Equipment", "stage" : "Retired", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : [], "score" : 0, "description" : "Auto-retired 2026-10-08: dropped by the sector cap — no member passed the membership test for 'U.S. Oil Refiners & Refining Margin Expansion' (prior stage Nascent, 3 tickers).", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Brazil Fintech & Digital Banking Rally", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["PAGS","STNE","NU","XP","INTR","ITUB"], "score" : 78.9, "description" : "The rally is being driven by Brazil’s election shock: Flávio Bolsonaro finished ahead of President Lula in the October 4 first round, lifting hopes for a more market-friendly, fiscally disciplined government and reducing perceived political risk. The October 25 runoff remains uncertain, so the move is largely a repricing of expectations rather than a settled outcome.", "rs_avg" : 97.9}, {"name" : "Product Tanker Shipping", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : "Crude & Product Tanker Shipping", "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["TRMD","TNK","STNG","HAFN","ASC"], "score" : 78.9, "description" : "The rally is being driven by a historic spike in tanker freight rates, as Middle East conflict and Strait of Hormuz disruptions extend routes and tie up vessel capacity. VLCC rates have topped $1 million per day on some routes, sharply improving earnings prospects for tanker owners.", "rs_avg" : 97.8}, {"name" : "Vaccine Developers Bacterial & Respiratory", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["PCVX","NVAX","MRNA"], "score" : 78.8, "description" : "PCVX is jumping on strong Phase 3 results for Vaxcyte’s VAX-31 pneumococcal vaccine, which met all primary endpoints and showed competitive immune responses versus existing shots. NVAX and MRNA have been swept up in a broader vaccine-stock rally after reports of a Russian lab worker’s death raised speculation about outbreak preparedness and possible government purchases; the plague risk has since been described as low, so that catalyst is fragile.", "rs_avg" : 97.6}, {"name" : "Customer Engagement & Marketing/CX SaaS Platforms", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : "AI-Powered Enterprise Analytics & Intelligent Workflow SaaS", "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["AMPL","KVYO","BRZE","FRSH","HUBS"], "score" : 78.6, "description" : "There isn’t one clear shared catalyst: FRSH is rising on its announced addition to the S&P SmallCap 600, which can prompt buying by index-tracking funds. BRZE is benefiting from upbeat analyst/customer commentary and new AI product announcements at its Braze Forge conference; AMPL appears to be extending a momentum rally after beating Q2 revenue estimates and hitting a 52-week high, with no fresh catalyst identified in the available reports.", "rs_avg" : 97.2}, {"name" : "Enterprise Unstructured Data Storage Infrastructure", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["DBX","QMCO","BOX"], "score" : 78.5, "description" : "BOX’s move appears to reflect follow-through from its strong Q2 results and bullish analyst commentary on AI-driven demand and Enterprise Advanced seat expansions and pricing. QMCO is rallying after a major earnings beat: it posted $0.18 adjusted EPS versus expectations for a loss, on revenue above forecasts, its first adjusted profit since 2023.", "rs_avg" : 97.1}, {"name" : "Cloud Contact Center & CCaaS Communication Platforms", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["TWLO","RNG","FIVN","NICE"], "score" : 78.3, "description" : "There doesn’t appear to be one confirmed headline catalyst across all four. The available reporting points to broader AI/tech-sector buying for RNG, while TWLO has its own S&P 500 inclusion and AI-growth narrative; I can’t verify a specific fresh catalyst for FIVN and NICE.", "rs_avg" : 96.7}, {"name" : "Network Security & Zero-Trust Edge", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["NET","FFIV","RPD","PANW","CHKP","NTSK","VRNS","S","ZS","TENB","FTNT","QLYS","CRWD","OKTA"], "score" : 78.3, "description" : "The main catalyst is a sector-wide re-rating around AI-agent security: as companies deploy autonomous AI agents, investors expect cybersecurity spending to rise. CrowdStrike’s AI-security initiatives and upbeat commentary from cybersecurity executives reinforced the theme; Okta also had company-specific optimism around its outlook.", "rs_avg" : 96.5}, {"name" : "Marketing & Digital Presence SaaS Platforms", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["WIX","ZETA","GDDY","SPT"], "score" : 77.9, "description" : "ZETA’s clearest catalyst is its announced acquisitions of Senso and Digital Audience, plus anticipation of product and partnership updates at its Oct. 8 Zeta Live event. I don’t see a comparable fresh company-specific catalyst for WIX or GDDY; any gains there appear more likely tied to broader software-sector strength and sentiment than a shared headline.", "rs_avg" : 95.8}, {"name" : "Genomics & DNA Sequencing Tools", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["WGS","QGEN","NTRA","ILMN","GRAL","BRKR","TXG","TWST","GH"], "score" : 77.8, "description" : "There isn’t one shared catalyst: the group appears to be riding a broader genomics/AI enthusiasm trade. GRAL has a distinct boost from the FDA advisory panel’s favorable vote on its Galleri cancer test; ILMN also got analyst price-target hikes tied to expected clinical-sales improvement.", "rs_avg" : 95.5}, {"name" : "Bitcoin Treasury & Crypto Proxy Equities Correlation Basket", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["SBET","MSTR","PURR","BMNR"], "score" : 77.7, "description" : "The main driver is a crypto-risk-on rebound: Bitcoin and Ethereum are climbing, helped by easing Treasury yields, renewed ETF demand and short-covering, lifting MSTR, BMNR and SBET as crypto proxies. PURR is riding bullish sentiment around Hyperliquid and its HYPE-token treasury; there’s no clear fresh company-specific catalyst shared by all four.", "rs_avg" : 95.4}, {"name" : "Cloud Application Delivery & Observability Infrastructure", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["DDOG","FSLY","ATEN","DT"], "score" : 77.5, "description" : "DT and DDOG are benefiting from renewed enthusiasm for AI observability, analyst upgrades, and expectations that enterprise AI workloads will drive monitoring spend. FSLY’s catalyst is Comcast deploying Fastly’s delivery software for Peacock live sports, alongside its AI-security push; I don’t have a confirmed specific catalyst for ATEN in the available news.", "rs_avg" : 95.1}, {"name" : "Data Backup & Cyber Resiliency Software", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : "Network Security & Zero-Trust Edge", "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["CVLT","RBRK","BLZE","AVPT"], "score" : 77.3, "description" : "There doesn’t appear to be one fresh headline driving all three. The move looks like a cybersecurity/data-resilience trade: Rubrik’s strong quarterly results and analyst optimism, Commvault’s new AI-protection tools and a higher Scotiabank price target, with Backblaze likely participating in the same sector momentum.", "rs_avg" : 94.7}, {"name" : "Enterprise Server, Storage & Data Infrastructure Hardware", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["SMCI","STX","DELL","ANET","CSCO","HPE","NTNX","NTAP"], "score" : 77.1, "description" : "The main driver is renewed AI-data-center infrastructure demand: Supermicro’s NetApp partnership and Nvidia rack shipments, HPE’s large AI-server order and stronger networking outlook, and continued expectations for server and storage spending. The gains across the group look like a broader rotation into AI hardware, not one catalyst shared by every company.", "rs_avg" : 94.1}, {"name" : "Cloud Data Storage & Analytics Infrastructure", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["MDB","SNOW","ESTC"], "score" : 77, "description" : "There’s no single catalyst: the shared tailwind is renewed optimism about enterprise AI and AI-agent workloads boosting demand for data platforms, reinforced by Bernstein’s bullish view of MongoDB. Elastic also got a fresh boost from Gartner naming it a Leader in Enterprise AI Search; Snowflake’s strength appears tied to its accelerating AI-related consumption and recent raised outlook.", "rs_avg" : 94.1}, {"name" : "Management & Business Process Consulting Services", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["EXLS","CRAI","ACN","HURN","ICFI"], "score" : 77, "description" : "The main catalyst is Accenture’s strong Q4 earnings and record bookings, which eased fears that AI is undermining consulting demand and lifted the broader services sector. HURN and EXLS appear to be benefiting from that read-through; CRAI’s move has less clearly identified company-specific news.", "rs_avg" : 94}, {"name" : "Leisure & Recreation Discretionary Rebound", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["ASO","MAT","CCL","HAS","LIND"], "score" : 76, "description" : "CCL is rallying on a Q3 earnings beat, raised profit guidance and record bookings; MAT on reported takeover interest above $20 a share, amplified by activist pressure to explore strategic options. I don’t have enough verified current news to identify the specific catalysts for ASO, LIND and HAS.", "rs_avg" : 91.9}, {"name" : "Semiconductor Test, Yield & Assembly Supply Chain", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["PDFS","TER","CAMT","COHU","FORM","NVMI"], "score" : 75.5, "description" : "There’s no single confirmed company-specific headline: the move appears to be a sector-wide rotation into AI semiconductor testing and inspection, on expectations of stronger data-center, HBM, and advanced-packaging demand. Aehr’s recent AI-chip and silicon-photonics orders add a specific tailwind; the other names are largely riding the broader theme.", "rs_avg" : 91.1}, {"name" : "Alternative Asset Managers & Private Markets Platforms", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["PAX","PS"], "score" : 75.3, "description" : "Assuming you mean Pershing Square (NYSE: PS), there’s no clear company-specific catalyst in the available reports; the recent rise appears to be momentum rather than a confirmed news-driven move.", "rs_avg" : 90.6}, {"name" : "AI-Driven Memory & Storage Supply Shortage", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["TSM","MRVL","MU","AMD","NVDA","SKHY"], "score" : 75.2, "description" : "The shared catalyst is renewed optimism about a durable AI-infrastructure spending boom, with tight chip and memory supply reinforcing expectations for strong demand. Specific boosts include Marvell’s sharply higher long-term targets, AMD’s forecast of expanded 2027 supply, and upbeat AI-memory demand expectations; SK Hynix, however, has faced earnings caution ahead of results.", "rs_avg" : 90.4}, {"name" : "Digital Dollar & Crypto Payments Infrastructure", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["PYPL","USDE"], "score" : 75.2, "description" : "PYPL’s rise looks driven mainly by renewed optimism that branded checkout has stabilized, alongside growth in Venmo and Braintree and PayPal’s cost-cutting and AI-commerce push. There’s no clear single new catalyst this week; a new Venmo credit-card cash-back feature may also have helped sentiment.", "rs_avg" : 90.5}, {"name" : "Fintech Payments, Prepaid & Consumer Digital Banking Apps", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["DAVE","RELY","PAYS"], "score" : 75.2, "description" : "RELY’s move is mainly tied to William Blair adding Remitly to its October Analyst Conviction List, citing its valuation and growth outlook after a pullback. A broader rally in software-infrastructure peers also helped; there’s no comparable fresh company announcement identified.", "rs_avg" : 90.3}, {"name" : "AI-Powered Enterprise Analytics & Intelligent Workflow SaaS", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["PEGA","APPN","MSFT","PLTR","SAP","ASAN","NOW","PD","WK","INTA","CRM","PATH","DOCU","AI"], "score" : 74.7, "description" : "The shared catalyst is a broad rebound in growth and software stocks: soft U.S. jobs data reduced expectations for another Fed rate hike, while renewed AI optimism lifted tech sentiment. Software-sector gains also reflect stronger earnings expectations and easing concerns that AI will disrupt established software companies.", "rs_avg" : 89.4}, {"name" : "Vertical Commerce & Tax/Payments Software-Fintech Platforms", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["WSE","VERX","SHOP","GLBE"], "score" : 74.7, "description" : "SHOP (ecommerce merchant tools), VERX (tax compliance software) and WSE (cross-border payments) are showing strong RS as software and fintech platforms tied to transaction flow. WSE shows sharp recent RS acceleration. This is a weak, loosely connected cluster, proposed for human review.", "rs_avg" : 89.4}, {"name" : "Cloud Application Software Rotation (Oversold Turning Up)", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["PCOR","APPF","DUOL"], "score" : 74.6, "description" : "PCOR’s jump is tied to the Schneider Electric–PTC deal, which revived takeover speculation in software and put Procore in the spotlight as a potential acquisition target. I don’t see a matching news catalyst for DUOL or APPF; their moves look more like broader software-stock trading than a shared company-specific trigger.", "rs_avg" : 89.2}, {"name" : "Commercial, Office & Home Furniture Retailers and Manufacturers", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["HNI","ARHS","MLKN","W","WSM"], "score" : 74.6, "description" : "The move looks like a sector-wide rebound in home-furnishings sentiment, not one fresh catalyst: investors are responding to recent earnings beats and upbeat growth outlooks, especially Arhaus’s results and Wayfair’s strong Q2 and Q3 guidance. Lower expectations for interest rates may also be helping discretionary, housing-linked names.", "rs_avg" : 89.2}, {"name" : "Cloud Supply Chain & Warehouse Management Software", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["MANH","SPSC","DSGX"], "score" : 74.4, "description" : "There’s no clear shared headline catalyst: MANH’s move appears tied to its new Manhattan Active “Editions” cloud-platform tiers and bullish analyst sentiment, while DSGX has highlighted new supply-chain AI tools and received supportive analyst reiterations. I found no distinct fresh SPSC catalyst in the available coverage, so its strength may be sector or momentum-driven rather than news-specific.", "rs_avg" : 88.8}, {"name" : "For-Profit Postsecondary & Vocational Education", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["CVSA","LOPE","LAUR","STRA","PRDO"], "score" : 74.3, "description" : "There’s no clear single headline catalyst: the moves appear to reflect renewed optimism about education-sector demand and earnings, with STRA’s recent Zacks upgrade adding a company-specific boost. CVSA’s recent results beat estimates, but LOPE’s main fresh news was only its earnings-date announcement, so the broader move may also be sector momentum rather than a new event.", "rs_avg" : 88.6}, {"name" : "Life Science Tools & Analytical Instruments", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["CRL","ICLR","RVTY","IQV","MTD","WAT","A","MEDP","DHR","TMO","BIO","AZTA","RGEN","AVTR","MLAB"], "score" : 74.3, "description" : "There doesn’t appear to be one shared news catalyst across all six: the move looks like a life-sciences/tools sector rebound, with investor optimism about accelerating market growth and upcoming earnings. Company-specific headlines include Danaher’s planned AI-powered autonomous lab and Repligen’s completed BioLife acquisition; those don’t explain the whole group’s gains.", "rs_avg" : 88.6}, {"name" : "mRNA Vaccine & Personalized Cancer Therapy Platforms", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["MRK","BNTX","MRNA","ARCT"], "score" : 74.1, "description" : "The main catalyst is the strong Phase 3 melanoma results for Moderna’s personalized cancer vaccine, intismeran, combined with Merck’s Keytruda, which reduced recurrence or spread versus Keytruda alone. This week, Moderna’s Nasdaq-100 inclusion is adding buying demand; investors are also anticipating the full trial data at an oncology conference later this month.", "rs_avg" : 88.2}, {"name" : "AI data-center power buildout", "stage" : "Accelerating", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["TLN","GNRC","VST","ALAB","AGX","VICR","CEG"], "score" : 74, "description" : "The main catalyst is renewed AI/data-center power demand: Google’s 20-year agreement with Constellation to add 890 MW of nuclear capacity is lifting CEG and, by read-through, VST and TLN. ALAB is riding broader AI-chip enthusiasm and optimism about its Scorpio product ramp; VICR’s move is tied to higher revenue guidance from licensing royalties. I don’t see a clear new GNRC-specific catalyst in the available reports.", "rs_avg" : 88}, {"name" : "Digital Advertising & Ad-Tech Monetization Platforms", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["MGNI","DV"], "score" : 74, "description" : "DV’s catalyst is its new ChatGPT ad-attribution launch and OpenAI brand-suitability pilot, positioning it to measure a new advertising channel. MGNI’s move appears tied to its HP TV+ ad-tech win and renewed optimism about Google ad-tech remedies benefiting independent platforms.", "rs_avg" : 88}, {"name" : "Post-Acute & Home-Based Healthcare Services", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["CHE","OPCH","NHC","PACS","ADUS","PNTG"], "score" : 73.8, "description" : "The shared backdrop is a rotation/bid into home-based and post-acute care, with Option Care Health’s announced $5.8 billion buyout by McKesson and CD&R likely adding sympathy momentum. The available news points to no single deal catalyst for NHC, CHE, ADUS, PACS and PNTG.", "rs_avg" : 87.7}, {"name" : "Semiconductor Design, Test & Assembly Enablement Tools", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["CDNS","KLIC","SNPS","KEYS"], "score" : 73.8, "description" : "The common theme is AI-chip infrastructure: Synopsys’ upbeat growth outlook and OpenAI/AWS deals, plus TSMC and AI-design developments at Cadence, have lifted sentiment across chip-design and equipment names. Keysight is benefiting from strong AI-data-center test demand and bullish analyst coverage; KLIC has its own AI advanced-packaging story and strong results, though its latest weekly move appears modest.", "rs_avg" : 87.6}, {"name" : "Emerging Medical Device Innovators Breakout", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["INSP","ITGR","ATEC"], "score" : 73.6, "description" : "There isn’t one clear shared catalyst: INSP is reacting to AMA approval of dedicated Category I billing codes for Inspire V, effective in 2028. ATEC has no obvious company-specific news catalyst in the available reports; ITGR’s support is likely the KKR $127-per-share buyout and progress clearing antitrust review.", "rs_avg" : 87.2}, {"name" : "U.S. Apparel & Fashion Recovery", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["VSXY","SHOO","M","URBN","ANF","AEO","FIGS","RL","GAP","BKE","CROX","ROST","WWW","KSS","DDS","PVH"], "score" : 73.6, "description" : "There doesn’t appear to be a single company-specific catalyst; the move looks like a broad retail/consumer-stock lift as oil prices and Treasury yields eased, supporting risk appetite. Recent shopping-sales data also pointed to resilient consumer demand, though it’s not clear that this was the direct trigger for all six stocks.", "rs_avg" : 87.1}, {"name" : "IT Consulting & Business Process Outsourcing Services", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["EPAM","EXLS","G","ACN","CTSH","DXC","GIB"], "score" : 73.5, "description" : "The rally is a read-through from Accenture’s fiscal Q4 beat: revenue topped guidance, bookings hit $22.2 billion, and its FY2027 growth outlook was reassuring. Investors are treating that as evidence that AI-related work is boosting—not wiping out—demand for IT consulting and services across the sector.", "rs_avg" : 87}, {"name" : "AI Data Center High-Speed Interconnect & Signal Integrity Chipmakers", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["APH","COHR","BDC","CRDO","ALAB","GLW","LITE"], "score" : 73.3, "description" : "The main catalyst is a renewed AI-data-center optics trade: reports of possible U.S. restrictions on Chinese optical transceivers could benefit domestic suppliers, while Bernstein’s bullish LITE/COHR coverage and Coherent’s PhotonLink launch added momentum. ALAB and CRDO are participating in the broader AI connectivity rally; APH and GLW are sympathy plays on rising data-center networking demand.", "rs_avg" : 86.6}, {"name" : "Cross-Industry Test, Measurement & Design-Verification Tools", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["VIAV","CDNS","KEYS","AME"], "score" : 72.8, "description" : "There isn’t one shared headline catalyst: VIAV and KEYS are benefiting from AI-related data-center/network testing demand and fresh product news, including Keysight’s agentic-AI design tools. CDNS has support from its expanded TSMC advanced-node collaboration and AI-chip design launches; AME’s move looks more like analyst target increases and earnings-estimate upgrades than a new company announcement.", "rs_avg" : 85.5}, {"name" : "Restaurant Chain Recovery", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["DRI","CAKE","SHAK","BJRI","EAT","CBRL","WING","FWRG"], "score" : 72.6, "description" : "This looks like a broad casual-dining rebound rather than one shared headline: investors are responding to better-than-feared restaurant sales and renewed confidence in consumer demand. BJRI has a specific boost from Mizuho’s upgrade and stronger Q3 same-store-sales checks; the move in the other names appears more sentiment-driven.", "rs_avg" : 85.3}, {"name" : "Defensive Consumer Rotation & Trade-Down", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["TGT","COST","DG","WMK","BJ","GO","OLLI","KR","DLTR"], "score" : 72.5, "description" : "There’s no clear single catalyst across the group: recent coverage points to Target and Dollar General benefiting from tariff-refund-driven margin support, while Ollie’s had an earnings beat and BJ’s Wholesale had strong results. I don’t see a matching news trigger in the available information for Weis Markets or Kroger, so the broader move may reflect rotation into value-oriented retailers rather than one headline.", "rs_avg" : 85}, {"name" : "Energy Supply Disruption: Middle East Geopolitical Risk", "stage" : "