ading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["MBX","PTGX","CORT"], "score" : 71.3, "description" : "PTGX’s lift appears tied to optimism around its milestone-and-royalty revenue stream, FDA-approved ICOTYDE, and the upcoming rusfertide decision—not a clearly identified new catalyst this week. CORT is benefiting from strong Q2 results, raised 2026 revenue guidance, and optimism about its oncology drug Lifyorli’s European approval prospects.", "rs_avg" : 82.5}, {"name" : "Lodging & Hotel REITs", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["PK","PEB","DRH","APLE","RHP","RLJ","SHO"], "score" : 71.2, "description" : "There doesn’t appear to be a single fresh company-specific headline behind the group’s move. The likely driver is a broader bid for hotel REITs, supported by resilient lodging demand and recent upbeat operating results; the available news doesn’t establish a more specific catalyst this week.", "rs_avg" : 82.5}, {"name" : "Fintech & Digital Finance Sector Re-rating on Fed Easing", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["V","MA","MQ","PYPL","STNE","AFRM","PAGS","KSPI","CPAY","NCNO","FLYW","EVTC","BR","DLO","ACIW","CHYM","QTWO","JKHY","XYZ"], "score" : 71, "description" : "The clearest catalyst is Brazil’s first-round presidential vote: Flávio Bolsonaro’s lead sparked a sharp rally in PagSeguro (PAGS) and likely helped lift Brazilian fintech peer BR. Chime (CHYM) also had a William Blair analyst-list boost; I don’t see a confirmed single company-specific catalyst tying together KSPI, MQ, and MA.", "rs_avg" : 82}, {"name" : "Specialty P&C Insurance Underwriters Rotation Reversal", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["ACGL","SKWD","PGR","EG","HCI","SLDE","THG","TRV","CB","SPNT","WRB","PLMR","AFG","RNR","HG","AIG","KMPR","MCY"], "score" : 70.6, "description" : "There’s no clear single company-specific headline tying all six together; th