","IAG","NEM","SSRM","RGLD","CDE","AG","EXK","PAAS","ASM","HMY","MUX"], "score" : 62.9, "description" : "The move appears to be a broad precious-metals trade, not a single company catalyst: gold has found support from safe-haven demand amid French and U.S. fiscal/bond-market worries, alongside softer rate-hike expectations and intermittent easing in the dollar and Treasury yields. Those factors are lifting gold and silver exposure across miners and royalty companies.", "rs_avg" : 65.7}, {"name" : "Diabetes Management Devices (CGM, Insulin Pumps & Delivery)", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : "Medical Device Mean-Reversion & Rotation Recovery", "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["MMED","BBNX","DXCM"], "score" : 62.7, "description" : "The catalysts are mixed: DXCM is getting a lift from Barclays’ new Overweight rating and $115 target, while MMED’s recent optimism centers on its raised FY2027 growth outlook and Medtronic separation-related activity. I don’t see a positive BBNX catalyst in the available news—recent headlines concern safety issues and class-action lawsuits, so its rise may be a rebound or trading momentum.", "rs_avg" : 65.3}, {"name" : "Bank Stocks: Rising-Rate NIM Expansion", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["NBTB","BBVA","SAN","CBC","MUFG","HOPE","FIBK","NIC","FBNC","CLBK","NBN","AMAL","WABC","FCF","SMFG","NWG","ING","TRMK","CATY","OSBC","FITB","QCRH","MFG","C","OFG","HWC","HIFS","STBA","DCOM","HOMB","SFNC","NWBI","CVBF","RBCAA","WFC","JPM","CHCO","FSUN","FBP","BUSE","CBSH","PFBC","UBSI","ESQ"], "score" : 62.1, "description" : "There’s no clear shared company-specific headline in the available information; the likely common driver is a broader bank-stock rebound on expectations that rates stay higher, supporting lending income. The move isn’t confirmed by the available reports, and higher Treasury yields and a flatter yield curve could also pressure bank margins.", "rs_avg" : 64.3}, {"name" : "Insurance Brokerage & Employee Benefits Advisory", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["BRO","MRSH","WTW","AJG"], "score" : 61.5, "description" : "There’s no clear shared news catalyst: the moves look more like a broker-sector bounce and stock-specific analyst sentiment. BRO got a bullish Oppenheimer initiation citing expected organic-growth recovery and Accession deal upside; MRSH’s recent headlines are restructuring and acquisitions, while AJG’s are niche expansion deals.", "rs_avg" : 63.1}, {"name" : "Regulated Electric Utilities Defensive Rotation", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["CNP","AEP","TXNM","AEE","SO","EVRG","LNT","ETR","PNW","IDA","WEC","OGE","DUK","NWE"], "score" : 61.4, "description" : "The move looks like a broad utility-sector sympathy rally, sparked by Google’s newly announced long-term nuclear-power deal with Constellation Energy for its data centers. It reinforced expectations that AI-driven electricity demand will benefit power companies; there’s no clear company-specific catalyst for all six names.", "rs_avg" : 62.7}, {"name" : "Precision Timing & Motion Control Component Makers", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["FEIM","SITM","ALNT"], "score" : 61.04, "description" : "There’s no single fresh catalyst: the moves appear to reflect continued enthusiasm for AI/data-center demand and recent strong results. SITM is riding 127% year-over-year revenue growth and its expanded timing business; ALNT’s support is its earnings and orders beat, while FEIM has no clear new headline catalyst and may be moving with broader tech/defense momentum.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Homebuilders & Residential Construction Supply Chain", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["SKY","BCC","PHM","CVCO","NVR","DHI","BXC","TOL"], "score" : 60.5, "description" : "The clearest shared catalyst is housing-sector optimism, with investors responding to analyst support for homebuilders—especially Morgan Stanley’s new Overweight rating and $159 target on Toll Brothers, citing resilient affluent buyers and an attractive valuation. TOL also announced a new Cary, North Carolina community, but there’s no single obvious headline linking all three stocks.", "rs_avg" : 61}, {"name" : "Class I Railroad Freight Carriers", "stage" : "Mainstream", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["UNP","CSX","NSC","CNI"], "score" : 60, "description" : "The main catalyst is renewed optimism around Union Pacific’s proposed $85 billion acquisition of Norfolk Southern: UP’s CEO voiced near-total confidence in regulatory approval, and the railroads highlighted customer support for the deal. That’s lifting UNP and NSC directly, with CSX moving alongside the broader railroad-sector optimism.", "rs_avg" : 60}, {"name" : "Semiconductor Process Instruments & RF/PCB Electronic Components", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["TTMI","SMTC"], "score" : 57.12, "description" : "MKSI process-control instruments and TTMI RF components and PCBs are riding the semiconductor and AI hardware build-out. Both are mid-RS suppliers outside existing themes.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Semiconductor Photomask & Ultra-Low-Power Chip Enablers", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["SYNA","PLAB"], "score" : 54.160000000000004, "description" : "AMBQ is benefiting from Jefferies’ new Buy rating and $90 target, reinforcing optimism about its edge-AI chips; SYNA is rallying after onsemi changed its takeover offer to $123 per share in cash. PLAB has no clear fresh catalyst in the available reports—its move may reflect broader semiconductor/AI interest and earlier analyst optimism after an earnings beat.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Space Economy: Satellite Communications & Launch Services", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["SPCX","RKLB"], "score" : 52.96000000000001, "description" : "The main shared catalyst is renewed enthusiasm for commercial space after Starship’s successful orbital flight, reinforced by bullish analyst commentary on SpaceX’s AI and launch prospects. Rocket Lab also has company-specific support from its Iridium acquisition plan, a large Synspective launch deal, and a Citi Buy rating; the move is not uniform, with yields and oil weighing on shares in some sessions.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "U.S. Domestic Passenger Airlines", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["DAL","LUV","AAL","UAL","ULCC"], "score" : 50.88, "description" : "The common lift appears to be falling oil prices and hopes that resilient travel demand and fare strength will offset fuel costs. DAL’s Oct. 9 earnings report is an additional near-term catalyst; there’s no clear shared company-specific headline for all three.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Business Development Companies & Private Credit Lenders", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["MAIN","ARCC","TRIN","FSK","HTGC","BXSL"], "score" : 47.44, "description" : "There’s no clear single headline catalyst: this looks more like a shared BDC-sector rebound, likely helped by sentiment around income-oriented lenders. Recent company-specific news doesn’t explain a coordinated rise—TRIN’s $350 million debt refinancing and earnings-date announcement weren’t positive price catalysts, while no fresh MAIN or BXSL catalyst appears in the available news.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Autonomous Vehicle & ADAS Technology Enablers", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["OUST","BB"], "score" : 44.928000000000004, "description" : "BB is rising on a strong earnings beat, raised FY27 guidance, and record QNX results, reinforced by major auto-software wins. OUST’s catalyst is its Seneca partnership to integrate Ouster lidar into autonomous wildfire-response drones, opening a new application for its sensors.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Global Agriculture Value Chain Recovery", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["CNH","AGCO","DE"], "score" : 44.480000000000004, "description" : "There doesn’t appear to be one clear, new headline driving all three higher. The move looks more like a sector-wide recovery trade on improving farm-equipment demand and hopes the agricultural cycle is bottoming, with added support from positive analyst commentary on AGCO and Deere’s strength in construction and compact equipment.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Aerospace Engine, Airframe Components & Defense Subsystem Suppliers", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["ARXS","DCO","ATI"], "score" : 44.160000000000004, "description" : "ATI is riding its raised 2026 outlook—especially higher free-cash-flow guidance—backed by strong aerospace and defense demand. I don’t see a clear fresh catalyst in the available information for DCO or DPC; DCO may be getting a read-through from the U.S. Navy’s large SM-6 missile contract, while DPC’s move appears unconfirmed.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Canadian Big Banks", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["RY","CM","BNS","TD"], "score" : 40.64000000000001, "description" : "The clearest company-specific catalyst is TD’s plan for a new C$10 billion share buyback and Scotiabank’s expanded buyback authorization to 40 million shares. CM doesn’t appear to have a comparable fresh catalyst, so its move is more likely tracking broader bank-sector strength.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Asset-Light Trucking & Freight Logistics Carriers", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["LSTR","ARCB","SAIA","KNX","RXO"], "score" : 38.32, "description" : "The rally appears tied to evidence of a tightening freight market: September data showed sharply contracting truck capacity and rising transportation prices, while truck shipments posted their first year-over-year increase since early 2023. The main tailwind is improving pricing power from scarce capacity—not a broad surge in freight demand.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Orthopedic Surgical Devices & Instruments", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : "Medical Device Mean-Reversion & Rotation Recovery", "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["SIBN","ZBH","CNMD"], "score" : 36.864000000000004, "description" : "There doesn’t appear to be one shared catalyst. SIBN is reacting to Jefferies raising its target and recent FDA clearance for its Onyx spinal-fusion system; CNMD’s recent earnings beat and higher full-year EPS guidance may be supporting it. ZBH’s move looks more like a rebound/analyst optimism ahead of earnings, rather than a fresh company announcement.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Inflammatory Disease & Immunology Biologics", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["AUPH","NRIX"], "score" : 33.99680000000001, "description" : "AUPH is benefiting from Q2 earnings that beat EPS expectations, despite weaker-than-expected revenue. NRIX’s catalyst is a two-year extension of its Gilead oncology research deal, bringing a $10 million fee; SYRE appears to be riding optimism around positive Phase 2 ulcerative-colitis data and its IBD pipeline, rather than a fresh announcement this week.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Steel & Aluminum Mill Producers", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["NUE","WS"], "score" : 29.337600000000005, "description" : "US steel mills and flat-rolled aluminum producers are rising in RS together, consistent with tariff/trade protection and pricing support for domestic metals.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Mobile SoC & Wireless Connectivity Semiconductors", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["QRVO","SWKS","QCOM"], "score" : 28.303360000000005, "description" : "The main catalyst is Skyworks and Qorvo receiving all regulatory clearances for their merger, with closing expected around October 5 and investors anticipating cost synergies. Qualcomm’s lift appears tied to broader chip-sector momentum and renewed optimism around its AI/data-center growth, rather than the merger itself.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Skilled Nursing & Senior Housing Healthcare REITs", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["LTC","WELL","OHI"], "score" : 27.402240000000006, "description" : "LTC Properties is rising on its push into senior-housing operations: it announced nearly $160 million in acquisitions of three communities, alongside divestitures expected to generate about $225 million in gains. RBC also raised its price target to $52 from $45 this week, adding support.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Emerging Quantum Computing Rally", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["INFQ","IONQ"], "score" : 26.70592000000001, "description" : "The group’s lift appears driven mainly by broad quantum-sector enthusiasm, including reports of roughly $2 billion in proposed federal grants for quantum technology and momentum around U.S. quantum funding. IONQ also has company-specific tailwinds from Bank of America’s new Buy rating and recent technical and customer-deployment news; the catalyst is less clearly tied to INFQ and QUBT individually.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Mortgage REITs (Agency & Residential MBS)", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["NLY","ORC"], "score" : 26.24, "description" : "I don’t see evidence of a single news catalyst shared by NLY, AGNC, ORC, and STWD; the available reports instead describe continued pressure on rate-sensitive real-estate stocks. If they’re higher this week, the likely common driver is a short-term bond-yield pullback or oversold rebound—not a confirmed company-specific announcement.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Bitcoin Miners Pivoting to AI Data Center Hosting", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["APLD","CORZ","CIFR"], "score" : 24.96, "description" : "It looks more like a sector-wide AI data-center/power trade than one catalyst shared by all four: investors are repricing former crypto miners as suppliers of scarce power and capacity for AI/HPC. APLD also has a Finland deal for access to up to 1 GW and earnings this week; those headlines may be lifting peers by association.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "U.S. Super-Regional & Midcap Commercial Banks", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["FITB","MTB","USB","ZION","CFG","HBAN","KEY","PNC","TFC","RF"], "score" : 24.040000000000003, "description" : "Ten large regional banks (MTB, USB, ZION, CFG, HBAN, KEY, PNC, TFC, RF, FITB) are moving in tight lockstep with residual correlation of 0.86. That points to a shared rate, credit and funding-cost driver rather than stock-specific news. Their RS is weak (22-36), so this looks like a group rotation or mean-reversion basket. It is split off from the broad NIM-expansion bank theme because these are US super-regional and midcap lenders.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Private Mortgage Insurance Underwriters", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["ESNT","NMIH","MTG"], "score" : 24, "description" : "No clear company-specific catalyst is evident; the move appears to be a broad rebound in mortgage insurers after recent sector weakness. ESNT’s modest Barclays price-target increase and AM Best’s affirmation of MGIC’s ratings may have helped at the margins, but neither explains all three rising together.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Regulated Utilities Wildfire & Rate-Case Exposure", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["EIX","PCG","SRE","AVA"], "score" : 15.360000000000003, "description" : "The move looks like a relief bounce and bargain hunting after heavy selloffs—not a fresh, clear-cut headline catalyst. California wildfire-liability concerns remain unresolved; PG&E’s undergrounding plan may be helping sentiment at the margin, but it hasn’t yet been approved.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Auto & Truck Dealership Retail Chains", "stage" : "Fading", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : ["LAD","ABG","AN","SAH"], "score" : 3.3600000000000003, "description" : "Publicly traded auto retail groups (LAD, ABG, AN, SAH) move together at depressed relative strength. They share exposure to new and used vehicle demand, floorplan financing costs and auto-loan credit. They could be an oversold rotation candidate if rates ease.", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "South African & Emerging-Market Gold Miners (Uncovered Producers)", "stage" : "Retired", "parent_theme" : "Precious Metals Miners—Gold & Silver Rally on Fed Easing", "source" : "live", "tickers" : [], "score" : 0, "description" : "Auto-retired 2026-10-08: thesis-merged into 'Precious Metals Miners—Gold & Silver Rally on Fed Easing' (ADR 0025 Arm B).", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Automotive Thermal & Powertrain Components Suppliers", "stage" : "Retired", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : [], "score" : 0, "description" : "Auto-retired 2026-10-08: retired — weak Fading at 2 members (< 3), #655 rule B — members released: BWA, MOD (prior stage Fading, 2 tickers at retirement).", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Bitcoin Mining Stocks Rotation Reversal", "stage" : "Retired", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : [], "score" : 0, "description" : "Auto-retired 2026-10-08: dropped during merge/absorption (no successor found) (prior stage Fading, 2 tickers).", "rs_avg" : null}, {"name" : "Branded Footwear & Apparel Brand Turnaround", "stage" : "Retired", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "live", "tickers" : [], "score" : 0, "description" : "Auto-retired 2026-10-08: retired — weak Fading at 2 member