ing synchronized RS improvement well ahead of broader energy sector recognition.", "rs_avg" : 74.75714285714285}, {"name" : "Branded Footwear & Hotel Consumer Discretionary Turnaround", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "shadow_promoted", "tickers" : ["VFC","ONON","HLT"], "score" : 72.7, "description" : "VFC, ONON and HLT are rising from very low RS levels. VFC and ONON share a branded footwear/apparel recovery, while HLT adds a travel-demand angle, so this cohort is a loose one.", "rs_avg" : 72.7}, {"name" : "Building Products & Home Improvement Materials Makers", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "shadow_promoted", "tickers" : ["MAS","PPG","FBIN","BCC"], "score" : 50.075, "description" : "MAS, PPG, FBIN and BCC are residential repair/remodel and building-products suppliers that have moved together with a 0.81 correlation. They share exposure to housing turnover, remodel demand and input costs, and may be rotating on rate-cut expectations. This is a more specific cohort than the broad homebuilders theme.", "rs_avg" : 50.075}, {"name" : "Data Analytics, AI Platform & Digital Transformation IT Services", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "shadow_promoted", "tickers" : ["TDC","GLOB","NAVN"], "score" : 63.4, "description" : "Data/AI platform and software-development services firms are catching a bid as enterprises spend on AI-enabled digital transformation.", "rs_avg" : 63.4}, {"name" : "Gene Editing & Specialty Biopharma Breakouts", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "shadow_promoted", "tickers" : ["NTLA","XERS","ERAS","PGNY"], "score" : 77.425, "description" : "Biotech names with sustained multi-week RS climbs from weak starts: NTLA (in vivo gene editing) and XERS (endocrine specialty pharma) point to speculative healthcare rotation.", "rs_avg" : 77.425}, {"name" : "Gold & Silver Miners Not Yet Classified (Mid-Tier & South African PGM/Gold Producers)", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "shadow_promoted", "tickers" : ["AGI","SBSW","HYMC"], "score" : 17.7, "description" : "Uncovered members of the precious-metals cluster (AGI gold producer, SBSW platinum/palladium/gold miner, HYMC gold/silver developer) are moving in lockstep with the broader miner group on strong residual correlation. They extend the precious-metals rally into producers and PGM names outside the existing basket.", "rs_avg" : 17.7}, {"name" : "Platinum Group & South African/Junior Precious Metals Miners", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "shadow_promoted", "tickers" : ["SBSW","NG","HYMC"], "score" : 12.166666666666666, "description" : "SBSW, NG and HYMC are precious and PGM-focused miners that sit in the gold/silver correlation cluster but are not in the existing precious metals theme. They are a small uncovered group driven by metal prices.", "rs_avg" : 12.166666666666666}, {"name" : "Regulated Electric & Gas Utilities Broad Defensive Rotation Extension", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "shadow_promoted", "tickers" : ["PEG","XEL","FE","NI","EXC","CMS","DTE"], "score" : 47.42857142857143, "description" : "A 19-stock utility cluster shows correlated moves; uncovered members PEG, XEL, FE, NI, EXC, CMS, DTE are regulated electric/gas utilities moving in lockstep with the covered defensive rotation group. Extending coverage to these names captures the same rotation into defensive yield.", "rs_avg" : 47.42857142857143}, {"name" : "Travel & Hospitality Lodging Brand Franchisors Rotation", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "shadow_promoted", "tickers" : ["HLT","PK","CCL"], "score" : 76.43333333333334, "description" : "HLT rose from RS 21 to 78 over four weeks as a hotel franchisor. This is an asset-light, fee-based lodging turn that parallels the lodging REIT theme. A related group is hotel and leisure travel operators with RS acceleration.", "rs_avg" : 76.43333333333334}, {"name" : "Work Management & Collaborative Design SaaS", "stage" : "Nascent", "parent_theme" : null, "source" : "shadow_promoted", "tickers" : ["MNDY","FIG","NAVN"], "score" : 59.5, "description" : "Collaboration and workflow software platforms (work management, UI/UX design) are showing relative strength as software rotation lifts workflow/collaboration names. Cohort is early with moderate RS.", "rs_avg" : 59.5}]}
